WEBVTT

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:29.154
"Free Beer"?

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.660
Free beer. Free beer.

00:00:35.177 --> 00:00:36.511
Free beer. Free beer.

00:00:36.595 --> 00:00:39.389
Free beer, beer, beer, beer, beer,
beer, beer, beer, beer, beer!

00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:40.682
Free...

00:00:55.072 --> 00:00:56.365
Ah!

00:00:56.448 --> 00:00:59.076
Hello. I'm here for the free beer.

00:00:59.368 --> 00:01:00.619
You got it.

00:01:00.702 --> 00:01:03.163
Right after these 800 people get it.

00:01:04.748 --> 00:01:06.667
Beer, beer-beer, beer, beer.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.002
Beer?

00:01:11.254 --> 00:01:13.006
Ah... yeah!

00:01:13.507 --> 00:01:16.093
Thank you, Headless Clone of Agnew.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:20.847
My fellow Earthicans, I'm proud
to announce I'm running for reelection

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:24.685
as president of Earth,
the greatest planet in the world.

00:01:24.935 --> 00:01:26.270
Yeah!

00:01:26.687 --> 00:01:29.189
Is everyone enjoying their free beer?

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:30.649
Yeah!

00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:34.403
Well, there's plenty more
where that came from.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.906
We're all out of beer.

00:01:41.576 --> 00:01:43.412
All right, listen up, nitwits.

00:01:43.495 --> 00:01:47.708
Who here is tired of illegal space aliens
taking our good Earth jobs?

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:52.587
Me, too. So, if I'm reelected,

00:01:52.671 --> 00:01:55.882
I promise to build
a really big Dyson fence

00:01:55.966 --> 00:01:58.510
across the southern border
of our solar system.

00:02:00.595 --> 00:02:04.599
And furthermore, by golly,
I promise to cut taxes for the rich

00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:08.562
and use the poor as a cheap
source of teeth for aquarium gravel.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.189
Yeah! That'll show those poor!

00:02:11.273 --> 00:02:13.900
Why are you cheering, Fry?
You're not rich.

00:02:13.984 --> 00:02:16.194
True, but someday I might be rich.

00:02:16.278 --> 00:02:18.447
And then people like me
better watch their step.

00:02:19.656 --> 00:02:21.116
Let's just find Bender.

00:02:26.163 --> 00:02:28.248
Ah, that hit the spot.

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:29.666
I found Bender!

00:02:34.171 --> 00:02:36.465
Good news, everyone.

00:02:36.548 --> 00:02:38.383
- What?
- I've repaired myself

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:42.346
with these convenient "Reelect Nixon"
ass stickers. Go, Nixon!

00:02:42.638 --> 00:02:45.682
Bender, you can't even vote.
You're a convicted felon.

00:02:45.974 --> 00:02:48.226
Convicted, sentenced and executed.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.104
But Nixon passed a law
that says ex-cons can vote again

00:02:51.188 --> 00:02:52.606
as long as they vote for Nixon.

00:02:52.731 --> 00:02:56.902
But Nixon's the worst president in history
and alternate history.

00:02:56.985 --> 00:02:59.071
The rest of you aren't voting for him,
are you?

00:02:59.154 --> 00:03:00.364
- Sure, we are!
- Why not?

00:03:00.989 --> 00:03:04.701
He may not be perfect, but do we
really want some unknown new guy?

00:03:04.826 --> 00:03:08.038
I'll stick with the evil maniac I know,
thank you.

00:03:08.246 --> 00:03:09.790
Well, I think we can do better.

00:03:09.873 --> 00:03:12.876
This year, I'm going to get involved
in the political process

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.920
and make my voice heard.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.713
What?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.389
Welcome to Debate 3012,

00:03:25.472 --> 00:03:30.060
the 3,012th debate
of the 3012 election year.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.895
We have a crowded field of candidates,

00:03:31.979 --> 00:03:34.606
so I will dispense
with the informal terrorizing

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:35.983
and begin the questions.

00:03:36.233 --> 00:03:37.943
Is this the political process?

00:03:38.026 --> 00:03:39.611
'Cause I'm here to get involved in it.

00:03:39.903 --> 00:03:40.988
Silence!

00:03:42.281 --> 00:03:46.618
Question one. Will you pledge today
to somehow reduce taxes

00:03:46.702 --> 00:03:48.912
while simultaneously lowering the deficit?

00:03:49.246 --> 00:03:50.956
Hey, that's a good idea. Sure.

00:03:51.039 --> 00:03:53.000
If it'll win me the election, then yes.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.295
We have a saying up in Alaska.

00:03:56.378 --> 00:03:57.713
That's all.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.048
Senator Travers?

00:04:00.299 --> 00:04:03.427
Look, let's be honest here.
No one likes taxes,

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.723
but they pay for our basic needs.
Roads, schools, defense.

00:04:07.931 --> 00:04:11.351
If we hope to realize our aspirations
as a great planet,

00:04:11.435 --> 00:04:15.689
we must each pay our fair share
to achieve those noble goals.

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.824
Thank you, Senator.
A thoughtful and lucid answer.

00:04:25.907 --> 00:04:27.701
You will be destroyed!

00:04:27.784 --> 00:04:30.787
Question two. The environment. Yes or no?

00:04:30.996 --> 00:04:32.706
No. It's junk science.

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:36.627
Two words. Condor attack.
Don't want that. Got to say no.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.047
Now, just a minute.
These are important issues.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.174
We can't just reduce them to sound bytes.

00:04:44.468 --> 00:04:46.136
According to reputable scientists...

00:04:48.472 --> 00:04:50.182
Enviromite!

00:04:58.148 --> 00:05:02.152
Hello? I'd like to volunteer.
Is anyone lurking?

00:05:05.822 --> 00:05:07.324
Hey, stop that.

00:05:09.034 --> 00:05:10.243
Senator Travers?

00:05:10.619 --> 00:05:12.162
That's no way to win an election.

00:05:12.371 --> 00:05:15.499
I give up.
No one cares about my message.

00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:18.710
I never should have used the same PR guy
as One Hour Hot Dog.

00:05:19.544 --> 00:05:23.507
People will wait for something good.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.175
No, don't quit.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.094
You have great ideas.

00:05:27.177 --> 00:05:29.596
You just need to get them out there
with social media.

00:05:30.847 --> 00:05:33.558
Look, I posted your debate video
on Facebag.

00:05:34.101 --> 00:05:35.852
10,000 views?

00:05:35.936 --> 00:05:38.438
That's more
than most water-skiing squirrels get.

00:05:38.522 --> 00:05:40.232
You really think I have a chance?

00:05:40.399 --> 00:05:41.775
Absolutely.

00:05:41.858 --> 00:05:46.196
We just need to conceal your intelligence
and honesty in a hipper, dumber package.

00:05:46.571 --> 00:05:48.365
Well, what have I got to lose?

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:50.951
I'm making you my new campaign manager.

00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:52.119
You, out!

00:05:52.327 --> 00:05:56.123
You haven't heard the last of...

00:06:01.211 --> 00:06:03.046
As the Iowa caucus approaches,

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:07.592
the state's hippest citizens
turned out for an old-fashioned flash mob.

00:06:08.802 --> 00:06:11.638
Chris Travers got a bump
in the New Hampshire polls today,

00:06:11.722 --> 00:06:15.767
where he simuldined in 250 diners at once
via hologram.

00:06:16.059 --> 00:06:18.729
This pie at this diner is the best pie.

00:06:21.773 --> 00:06:25.360
Chris Travers wins
the South California primary handily,

00:06:25.444 --> 00:06:28.697
thanks to a series of well-placed
cameo appearances.

00:06:30.032 --> 00:06:31.658
Super Tuesday is in the books,

00:06:31.742 --> 00:06:35.871
with Eurasia, Australia and Kentucky
turning out in big numbers.

00:06:36.079 --> 00:06:37.331
With the race a dead heat,

00:06:37.414 --> 00:06:40.542
it's all come down
to a final tally at the convention.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.383
And the first runner-up,

00:06:48.717 --> 00:06:53.180
who will take over if the nominee
is caughtwith a dead girl, a live boy

00:06:53.263 --> 00:06:55.474
or any kind of sexy ghost,

00:06:55.557 --> 00:06:57.142
Mr. Greenland!

00:07:01.021 --> 00:07:03.357
Which means our nominee is the senator

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.151
from the nation-state of Hawaii,

00:07:06.443 --> 00:07:07.903
Chris Travers!

00:07:10.614 --> 00:07:11.907
He won the nomination!

00:07:12.115 --> 00:07:13.825
We, the people, did it!

00:07:13.909 --> 00:07:16.828
It wasn't "we, the people,"
it was you, the mutant.

00:07:16.912 --> 00:07:19.456
Your insightful nagging
really won us over.

00:07:19.581 --> 00:07:23.919
Yeah. You explained his positions
in a way even an idiot could understand.

00:07:24.002 --> 00:07:26.338
And that appealed to me,
for whatever reason.

00:07:26.505 --> 00:07:29.007
Thanks, guys,
but we have a lot of work ahead of us.

00:07:29.216 --> 00:07:32.386
If we're going to win the election,
we've all got to get involved.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.304
- You said it!
- That's right.

00:07:34.596 --> 00:07:36.098
If you want my opinion,

00:07:36.181 --> 00:07:40.769
Nixon's only chance to defeat Travers
is with filthy lies, dirty tricks

00:07:40.852 --> 00:07:43.355
and good old Quaker thuggery.

00:07:43.438 --> 00:07:46.191
And I'm just the guy for the job.

00:07:59.705 --> 00:08:02.541
I'm not sure if it's safe to talk.
Are you wearing a wire?

00:08:02.708 --> 00:08:03.959
I'm 40% wire.

00:08:04.209 --> 00:08:05.627
Excellent. Now, listen.

00:08:05.711 --> 00:08:07.754
We got to get some dirt
on this Travers guy.

00:08:07.838 --> 00:08:09.464
Really McGovern him up.

00:08:09.548 --> 00:08:10.799
You know who McGovern was, right?

00:08:11.008 --> 00:08:12.759
I don't even know who you are.

00:08:22.603 --> 00:08:23.854
Hello, dirt.

00:08:24.563 --> 00:08:27.482
I'll start at "N" for nude pictures.

00:08:28.275 --> 00:08:30.611
Aw, Nobel Prize? That's no good.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.488
How about "A" for adultery?

00:08:34.239 --> 00:08:36.575
What? Straight-A transcript?

00:08:37.159 --> 00:08:39.911
Hey, what's that rifling sound?

00:08:39.995 --> 00:08:41.163
Uh-oh.

00:08:59.973 --> 00:09:02.726
All right.
I'm going to catch Travers on video

00:09:02.809 --> 00:09:04.853
at this sleazy strip club.

00:09:06.104 --> 00:09:08.857
In and out of the club
13 times in one night.

00:09:09.191 --> 00:09:11.109
- That's a record.
- Where's Travers?

00:09:11.193 --> 00:09:12.945
All I see is you going in and out.

00:09:13.028 --> 00:09:14.655
Yeah, me. I set the record.

00:09:16.073 --> 00:09:19.159
This is as useless as those pictures
you photoshopped.

00:09:19.242 --> 00:09:21.912
Look, just give me one more chance.
I got a source.

00:09:22.079 --> 00:09:25.832
Well, you did manage to get
a tremendous urine sample.

00:09:26.166 --> 00:09:28.126
Let's not talk about that.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.635
Is that you, Big Throat?

00:09:36.718 --> 00:09:38.303
In the flesh.

00:09:39.012 --> 00:09:41.598
Listen, I need some dirt
on Senator Chris Travers.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.141
How quaint.

00:09:43.225 --> 00:09:48.230
But I suppose I should do my part
for political intercourse.

00:09:48.313 --> 00:09:51.650
Come closer, and I'll expose what I know.

00:09:52.693 --> 00:09:53.735
There's nothing.

00:09:53.986 --> 00:09:56.822
He's as clean as a freshly waxed buttock.

00:09:57.072 --> 00:09:58.949
Hey! Did you put your tongue in my ear?

00:09:59.032 --> 00:10:01.368
Certainly not. I don't have a tongue.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.495
Oh, good. 'Cause I don't have an ear.

00:10:05.956 --> 00:10:07.624
Come on, come on, fall.

00:10:07.708 --> 00:10:09.501
Fall, damn it, fall!

00:10:10.127 --> 00:10:11.670
Well? What did you get on Travers?

00:10:11.837 --> 00:10:15.007
Is he a draft dodger? Sex offender?
Sex dodger?

00:10:15.215 --> 00:10:16.591
Nada. He's clean.

00:10:16.925 --> 00:10:21.555
I'm sorry, but there's not one unusual
thing about Senator Chris Zaxxar Travers.

00:10:21.888 --> 00:10:24.558
Wait, wait. His middle name is Zaxxar?

00:10:24.641 --> 00:10:26.101
Sounds kind of alien.

00:10:26.184 --> 00:10:27.352
The voters hate aliens.

00:10:27.603 --> 00:10:30.355
They sure do,
but this guy's as human as you or me.

00:10:31.189 --> 00:10:34.693
I don't care what he is.
We'll start a rumor that he's an alien.

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:37.029
Hey, yeah. That'll cost him votes.

00:10:37.154 --> 00:10:39.156
Then, when he says
he was born on this planet,

00:10:39.239 --> 00:10:41.408
we make him cough up
his Earth certificate.

00:10:41.533 --> 00:10:43.619
Keep it on the news,
put him on the defensive.

00:10:43.702 --> 00:10:49.082
Oh, this is sneaky.
I feel a jowl movement coming on.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.254
And that's how you end hunger.

00:10:54.588 --> 00:10:55.839
Does anyone have any questions?

00:10:55.922 --> 00:10:58.008
I do, I do! Me, Bender!

00:10:58.383 --> 00:11:00.761
Yes, the robot with the megaphone
jumping up and down.

00:11:01.219 --> 00:11:06.183
I have a question
for Senator C. Zaxxar Travers.

00:11:09.019 --> 00:11:11.063
Tell me, Zaxxar,

00:11:11.146 --> 00:11:13.357
were you even born on Earth?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.318
Because the Earth constitution
clearly states

00:11:16.401 --> 00:11:19.446
that only people born on Earth
can be president.

00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:21.865
Isn't that right,
Justice Ruth Bader Ginsburg?

00:11:21.949 --> 00:11:24.284
You Ruth Bader believe it!

00:11:24.576 --> 00:11:25.702
But I...

00:11:25.786 --> 00:11:27.537
Of course I was born on Earth.

00:11:27.829 --> 00:11:29.247
Oh, really?

00:11:29.331 --> 00:11:32.668
Then we voters demand
you release your Earth certificate

00:11:32.751 --> 00:11:34.544
so I can then claim it's a fake.

00:11:34.878 --> 00:11:37.547
I'm not going to dignify
this preposterous charge.

00:11:37.631 --> 00:11:39.299
Are there any real questions?

00:11:39.591 --> 00:11:41.593
Scoop Chang, Fox Quote-Unquote News.

00:11:41.802 --> 00:11:43.345
Senator, in the last 10 seconds,

00:11:43.428 --> 00:11:45.681
I've heard reports
you weren't actually born on Earth.

00:11:45.764 --> 00:11:47.391
Care to evade these compelling charges?

00:11:47.641 --> 00:11:49.309
No. I mean, yes.

00:11:49.393 --> 00:11:50.644
I mean...

00:11:54.273 --> 00:11:56.483
Okay, let's nip this
Earther movement in the bud

00:11:56.566 --> 00:11:58.151
by releasing your Earth certificate.

00:11:58.235 --> 00:11:59.319
Where were you born?

00:11:59.403 --> 00:12:01.238
Our Lady of Patriotism Hospital.

00:12:01.363 --> 00:12:03.323
Patriotism, good. Where is it?

00:12:03.657 --> 00:12:05.575
- Kenya.
- Cradle of humanity.

00:12:05.701 --> 00:12:09.371
Leela, this is just a stupid distraction
from the issues.

00:12:09.496 --> 00:12:12.332
Please don't look
for my Earth certificate.

00:12:12.666 --> 00:12:14.876
Hey! That was my favorite window.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.545
I better see what they want.

00:12:16.753 --> 00:12:18.588
We want an Earthling,

00:12:18.672 --> 00:12:20.799
not a dirty space thing!

00:12:20.882 --> 00:12:22.467
Why are you rednecks doing this?

00:12:22.759 --> 00:12:24.261
Leela, don't stereotype.

00:12:24.678 --> 00:12:26.471
Why are you yokels doing this?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.474
I may be just a backwoods septic tank,

00:12:29.558 --> 00:12:32.436
but I've had it up to here
with you foreigners.

00:12:32.644 --> 00:12:34.313
But I come from Earth.

00:12:34.521 --> 00:12:37.149
Then show us your Earth whatchacallit.

00:12:37.357 --> 00:12:40.694
Long-form certificate of live birth.

00:12:40.777 --> 00:12:42.738
What would it take to convince you people?

00:12:42.821 --> 00:12:44.948
Would I have to have been born
right before your eyes?

00:12:45.198 --> 00:12:46.450
It wouldn't hurts.

00:12:46.533 --> 00:12:47.784
Hit it, rubes!

00:12:47.909 --> 00:12:49.870
We don't want a foreigner!

00:12:49.953 --> 00:12:51.830
We want someone born here!

00:12:52.539 --> 00:12:54.249
I'm still working on that one.

00:12:56.043 --> 00:12:57.336
What's wrong with you?

00:12:57.419 --> 00:13:00.297
Why are you sabotaging a decent,
honest candidate?

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.424
'Cause they won't let me near
the Hoover Dam anymore.

00:13:02.507 --> 00:13:03.592
Ooh!

00:13:03.675 --> 00:13:05.761
What a bunch of xenophobes.

00:13:05.844 --> 00:13:08.180
It's time to find Senator Travers'
Earth certificate

00:13:08.263 --> 00:13:09.848
and put an end to this nonsense.

00:13:10.223 --> 00:13:12.434
Who wants to help me break
into the hospital in Kenya?

00:13:12.851 --> 00:13:15.979
I'll come.
As long as there's no xenophobes there.

00:13:17.272 --> 00:13:19.733
- I want to come, too.
- You? Why?

00:13:19.983 --> 00:13:23.278
To prove that I can put
divisive partisan politics aside

00:13:23.362 --> 00:13:25.280
to participate in a break-in.

00:13:37.376 --> 00:13:38.835
Hospital ho!

00:13:56.853 --> 00:13:58.355
Shh!

00:13:58.438 --> 00:14:00.440
It's a herd of night watchmen.

00:14:08.949 --> 00:14:10.242
I found it!

00:14:12.369 --> 00:14:15.289
I don't understand.
There's no Earth certificate in here.

00:14:15.414 --> 00:14:16.498
No, there isn't.

00:14:19.626 --> 00:14:21.670
I told you not to look.

00:14:22.045 --> 00:14:23.964
So, you're not from Earth after all.

00:14:24.214 --> 00:14:25.590
Of course I'm from Earth.

00:14:25.924 --> 00:14:28.302
Wait a second.
There's no Earth certificate,

00:14:28.427 --> 00:14:32.556
but it does say your mother was admitted
to the maternity ward. This morning!

00:14:35.142 --> 00:14:37.644
I should have known
the truth would come out sooner or later.

00:14:38.103 --> 00:14:41.440
The fact is, I really was born on Earth

00:14:41.523 --> 00:14:42.608
tomorrow.

00:14:42.691 --> 00:14:45.360
You see, I'm not from another planet.

00:14:45.444 --> 00:14:47.154
I'm from the future.

00:15:06.214 --> 00:15:08.717
This is crazy. You're from the future?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.180
Yes. I was sent back from the year 3028
to prevent Nixon from getting elected.

00:15:13.388 --> 00:15:18.101
I was sent forward from the year 2000,
but you don't hear me gassing on about it.

00:15:18.226 --> 00:15:20.896
But why would it be so important
to stop Nixon?

00:15:21.146 --> 00:15:24.024
Because of the horrific events
he's going to set in motion.

00:15:24.107 --> 00:15:25.484
Oh, God.

00:15:25.567 --> 00:15:27.569
I can't bring myself to describe it.

00:15:27.819 --> 00:15:29.655
Oh, well.
Want to hear about how I got frozen?

00:15:30.739 --> 00:15:31.865
Not really.

00:15:33.075 --> 00:15:34.826
It all started with Nixon's promise

00:15:35.911 --> 00:15:37.704
to build an alien-proof fence
around the solar system.

00:15:37.955 --> 00:15:41.416
Without cheap alien labor for menial jobs
like harvesting crops,

00:15:41.792 --> 00:15:42.876
teaching math,

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.879
and curing disease, the economy collapsed.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.883
Starvation. Desperation. Despair.

00:15:50.092 --> 00:15:52.010
So far, so good. Then what?

00:15:52.219 --> 00:15:54.805
Unable to feed
the world's starving masses,

00:15:54.888 --> 00:15:56.598
Nixon took bold action.

00:15:56.848 --> 00:16:00.602
In this time of crisis,
I call upon the soylent...

00:16:00.686 --> 00:16:02.646
I mean, silent majority.

00:16:11.613 --> 00:16:12.698
Still good.

00:16:12.781 --> 00:16:14.449
With the working class gone,

00:16:14.533 --> 00:16:17.619
robots were forced
to do all the menial labor.

00:16:20.455 --> 00:16:23.333
Before long, they rose up in revolt...

00:16:29.881 --> 00:16:33.593
Led by a bending unit
named B.B. Rodriguez.

00:16:36.972 --> 00:16:40.434
Wait...
I know a robot named B.B. Rodriguez!

00:16:40.726 --> 00:16:44.229
Wait... I am a robot named B.B. Rodriguez.

00:16:44.313 --> 00:16:45.939
So, I become ruler of Earth?

00:16:46.189 --> 00:16:47.190
Indeed.

00:16:47.274 --> 00:16:50.110
Yes! In your face,
high school guidance counselor.

00:16:50.527 --> 00:16:54.031
The robots crushed our most
treasured monuments and celebrities,

00:16:54.114 --> 00:16:56.825
but they couldn't crush the human spirit.

00:16:56.908 --> 00:16:58.076
We went into hiding,

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.538
and after careful research,
located a xeroxed copy

00:17:01.622 --> 00:17:04.333
of an ancient time travel code.

00:17:04.583 --> 00:17:05.959
Though I was only 15,

00:17:06.043 --> 00:17:09.504
mankind entrusted me
with its last remaining suit and tie

00:17:09.588 --> 00:17:11.381
and sent me back in time.

00:17:11.506 --> 00:17:13.216
I would be raised by my grandparents,

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.093
somehow get into Harvard Law School,

00:17:15.177 --> 00:17:17.346
become a community organizer, a senator,

00:17:17.596 --> 00:17:18.680
and finally,

00:17:18.764 --> 00:17:20.599
defeat Richard Nixon.

00:17:23.268 --> 00:17:25.771
I escaped just as the robots arrived.

00:17:27.397 --> 00:17:30.192
All right, I'm low on bullets.
Everybody, scooch together.

00:17:30.609 --> 00:17:33.028
It's not too late.
You can still win the election.

00:17:33.278 --> 00:17:35.489
No, I can't. The Earthers are right.

00:17:35.572 --> 00:17:37.157
I have no Earth certificate.

00:17:37.449 --> 00:17:39.952
But you will have one in just a few hours.

00:17:40.035 --> 00:17:41.787
And everyone will know it's real,

00:17:41.954 --> 00:17:45.040
'cause we'll broadcast
your birth on live TV.

00:17:46.458 --> 00:17:48.877
If it's on TV, it has to be real.

00:17:50.754 --> 00:17:53.590
Morbo interrupts Bowling For Quatloos

00:17:53.799 --> 00:17:57.886
to present breaking coverage
of the birth of Senator Chris Travers.

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.263
We now go live to the delivery room,

00:18:00.514 --> 00:18:02.182
where we're already at there.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:06.478
Ow!

00:18:06.561 --> 00:18:08.563
Back, please. She needs room.

00:18:08.689 --> 00:18:10.315
- Thanks.
- Not you.

00:18:10.399 --> 00:18:11.984
The camerawoman needs room.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.986
This is it, ladies and gentlemen.

00:18:14.069 --> 00:18:15.320
The candidate is...

00:18:15.404 --> 00:18:17.239
I believe he's crowning!

00:18:17.447 --> 00:18:19.616
Push, Mom, push. You can do it.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.995
I bet nothing comes out. Just you watch.

00:18:23.078 --> 00:18:24.830
Here comes the head.

00:18:24.913 --> 00:18:26.415
And now the neck.

00:18:26.707 --> 00:18:28.875
Linda, I'm down here at the pelvis,

00:18:28.959 --> 00:18:32.045
and folks round these parts
can't remember the last time

00:18:32.129 --> 00:18:36.091
a time-traveling senator
attended his own birth. Back to you.

00:18:36.425 --> 00:18:39.052
Thanks, Morbo. You be careful down there.

00:18:40.595 --> 00:18:42.889
And the candidate is born!

00:18:43.265 --> 00:18:46.852
We have a birth. Repeat, we have a birth.

00:18:49.605 --> 00:18:50.647
Aw...

00:18:50.731 --> 00:18:52.274
He's got his own eyes.

00:18:52.608 --> 00:18:54.443
Well, who'd have thunk it?

00:18:54.526 --> 00:18:58.113
He was born all right, just like he said.

00:19:06.997 --> 00:19:10.751
And with the polls now closed
in every time zone worldwide,

00:19:10.959 --> 00:19:13.795
from Tomorrowland
to the Republic of Yesterday,

00:19:13.879 --> 00:19:15.589
we are able to declare a winner.

00:19:15.839 --> 00:19:18.550
Chris Travers, who leapt backwards in time

00:19:18.634 --> 00:19:21.887
and ahead in the polls,
has defeated Richard Nixon.

00:19:24.389 --> 00:19:25.974
He did it! He did it!

00:19:27.059 --> 00:19:29.811
- Yes!
- Congratulations, Mr. President.

00:19:29.895 --> 00:19:31.521
It's all thanks to you, Leela.

00:19:31.605 --> 00:19:34.900
You stood by me
and exposed my private medical records,

00:19:34.983 --> 00:19:36.693
even after I begged you not to.

00:19:36.944 --> 00:19:38.195
Aw, thanks.

00:19:38.278 --> 00:19:41.531
Now, get up to that podium
and change the world.

00:19:41.615 --> 00:19:43.992
Too bad your pal Nixon lost, Bender.

00:19:44.076 --> 00:19:45.661
You must be pretty glorked off.

00:19:45.827 --> 00:19:48.455
Nope. I don't give a bag of butts
who won the election.

00:19:48.538 --> 00:19:49.706
Nothing's going to change.

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.875
What? How can you say that?

00:19:52.167 --> 00:19:53.961
Watch and learn.

00:19:56.505 --> 00:19:57.923
My fellow Earthicans,

00:19:58.006 --> 00:20:01.134
I am honored and humbled
to stand before you tonight

00:20:01.218 --> 00:20:03.136
as your next president.

00:20:03.387 --> 00:20:04.763
Together, we will...

00:20:04.846 --> 00:20:06.390
Hey, what's going on?

00:20:06.473 --> 00:20:08.100
What's happening?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.937
You see, since Nixon wasn't elected,

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.897
the robot uprising didn't happen

00:20:13.981 --> 00:20:16.566
and Travers never got sent back
from the future.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.735
It's Politics 101.

00:20:24.199 --> 00:20:25.534
And the votes are in.

00:20:25.742 --> 00:20:27.661
Richard Nixon, running unopposed,

00:20:27.744 --> 00:20:30.539
has been reelected by a narrow landslide.

00:20:30.664 --> 00:20:31.707
Say what?

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:33.542
My fellow Earthicans,

00:20:33.625 --> 00:20:36.753
I am honored and humbled
to gloat before you tonight

00:20:36.837 --> 00:20:39.256
as your next president.

00:20:39.589 --> 00:20:42.843
Wow, it really doesn't matter
who you vote for.

00:20:42.926 --> 00:20:46.388
At least we tried to make a difference
by supporting Senator...

00:20:46.471 --> 00:20:48.181
Senator...

00:20:48.265 --> 00:20:49.516
What was his name again?

00:20:49.599 --> 00:20:50.892
I don't remember.

00:20:50.976 --> 00:20:52.853
We never even left this building.

00:20:52.936 --> 00:20:54.021
What?

00:20:54.104 --> 00:20:57.482
Nixon always wins!